      ],
      "body_md": "**AFHDS and AFHDS 2A are not interchangeable names.** Small combat-robot receivers such as the FS2A and the integrated receivers in the Malenki Nano/HV and Catalyst use **AFHDS 2A**, so the transmitter must support that protocol. The FS2A is useful when you want discrete electronics: it is a 4-channel board about 11 x 25 mm and 1 g bare. Integrated boards save even more wiring by combining the receiver with motor controllers.\n\nThe FlySky FS-GT5 is a six-channel pistol transmitter using AFHDS 2A. Whatever transmitter/receiver pair you choose, verify that the robot fails safe with drive and weapon commands returning to a safe state when the transmitter is turned off or signal is lost. Test that behavior before installing a weapon."
