      "body_md": "A high-torque lifter servo should not automatically be powered from the receiver's ordinary 5V rail. The Repeat 40kg servo is specified at 7.4V, while its matching Micro Inline Servo BEC accepts a much higher main-battery voltage and provides a regulated 7.4V output. This separates the servo's high transient current from a small receiver BEC and makes the power path explicit. Always check the exact servo voltage and current requirements before choosing a BEC; a regulator's current rating and thermal duty cycle matter as much as its output voltage."
